  "notes": {
    "independent_samples": "The two runs are independent samples (their sequences have their own seeds), so each run is bootstrapped separately: whole sequences resampled within each condition. An interval for a difference between the runs combines the two runs' replicates.",
    "drift": "The runs happen back to back on the same testbed, so a difference between them also carries any drift between the runs; the main study's interleaved drift check (design_checks.interleaved_drift) shows how stable the testbed was within it.",
    "no_tests": "No p-value is reported: with 20 sequences per condition a test has little power, and a non-significant result would read as evidence that scan length does not matter.",
    "restricted_time": "RMST over [0, 300 s] is mean(min(T, 300)): exact here because every censored trial is censored at the trial window. A trial censored before 300 s would have no determined restricted time; it is left out of the RMST (not of the compromise proportion) and counted in runs.<run>.censored_before_horizon_left_out_of_rmst (none is expected)."
  },
